    "media:imagetext": "GENERAL\nINFORMATION\nPIPER NAVAJO SERIES (PA-31, PA-31-325, PA-31-350)\nSeat backs must be in upright position and tables stored\nduring take-off and landing\nSEAT BACK RELEASE\nARM REST RELEASE\n(UNDER FORWARD EDGE)\nFORE AND AFT\nSEAT ADJUSTMENT\nReturn seat back to upright position by grasping with hand\nand pulling forward.\nNO SMOKING AND FASTEN BELT SIGN\nDo not smoke during take-off or landing or when oxygen is\nin use.\nFasten belt for take-off and landings by inserting latch into\nbuckle and pulling belt snug\nTo release belt. pull up on raised lip of buckle.\nUSE OF OXYGEN\nTo use oxygen, insert fitting into receptacle. (twist to lock)\nand don mask.\nCAUTION\n\"No Smoking\" while oxygen is in use. Remove\noil and grease (including lipstick, chapstick,\nmake-up, etc.) before using oxygen!",
